DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\\nCost: Fre
 e\\nAges: 0-60 months\\nCategory: Play & Games\\n\\nWay to Play Days are h
 eld on the 2nd Friday of every month. This event allows parents and caregi
 vers to complete free health screenings including developmental\, dental\,
  vision\, and/or speech. Local child development experts are on site to pr
 ovide information and assist grown-ups with questions they may have regard
 ing their child’s development.\nPlay Partner:\nLaura Petix\, MS OTR/L\, 
 Founder\, CEO The OT Butterfly LLC\nBook: The Sensory Code \nLaura Petix 
 is a licensed pediatric Occupational Therapist\, a neurodivergent mom rais
 ing a neurodivergent daughter\, and a passionate advocate for neurodiversi
 ty inclusion. Through her clinical expertise and lived experience\, she he
 lps parents understand how the nervous system shapes behavior and discover
  sensory strategies that support learning and engagement in daily life.\\n
 \\nMore info: https://www.pretendcity.org/events/way-to-play-day-2026-12-1
 1/
LOCATION:Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\, 29 Hubble\, Irvine\, CA
 \, 92618
URL:https://www.pretendcity.org/events/way-to-play-day-2026-12-11/
